      "writtenOn": "2024-10-24T21:08:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my understanding, comparing sample values is fragile. For example, if the test signal is random noise with average sample values are within [-0.5, 0.5], but there is one sample peaking at `1.0`, then our expected maximum value will be around sample maximum, but in our capture, since it by design has much less resolution, this one off peak in the test signal may not present. And that\u0027s OK because it does not contribute much to the power of the signal. That\u0027s why I was mentioning before that we should really be comparing the power or energy (normalized power), depending on the measurement mode, to have more reliable validation of the capture.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 303,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 304,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "4cb33ddbde59d1cdf93f2bc92637da19c8c017db",
